sys/libnh: catch up with sys/unix/unixmain.c so upstream's WebAssembly build links

Upstream's web build (make CROSS_TO_WASM=1) uses sys/libnh/libnhmain.c in
place of sys/unix/unixmain.c. At NetHack 5.0.0 it has fallen behind:

- after_opt_showpaths() moved to src/earlyarg.c, but libnhmain.c still
  defines it (duplicate symbol at link time); removed here, with
  opt_terminate(), which only it used;
- src/earlyarg.c calls whoami() as an external function; libnhmain.c's is
  static (an undefined symbol, hidden by ERROR_ON_UNDEFINED_SYMBOLS=0 until
  it aborts at run time); made external, as in unixmain.c;
- src/allmain.c calls get_nhuuid() and free_nhuuid(), defined only in
  unixmain.c; added here as unixmain.c has them without NHUUID.

No game rules change. Not submitted upstream (AI-assisted change).

